**Decisions the BRD didn't specify**
- **Journey shape** — five numbered steps with the net amount on its own screen before review, so REQ-006's "before lodgment" is literal.
- **BR-04 cents** — any decimal point is refused, including `.00`. "Cents are not accepted" read strictly.
- **BR-04 12 digits** — counted after stripping leading zeros (value-based reading).
- **BR-05/BR-06 boundaries** — equality passes; only strictly greater is refused. Skipped when the compared label is itself already refused.
- **BR-03** — "structurally valid" implemented as local@domain.tld; no MX/deliverability check.
- **Refusal wording** — the rule code is a chip inside the message text (e.g. `BR-01 Enter the ABN…`), plus a non-colour `!` icon and a `role="alert"` summary naming the rules (NFR-02/03).
- **NFR-04 scroll notice** — a permanently reserved 24px strip; text swaps between "more below" and "end of this screen". Reserved always so toggling can never shift or clip layout.
- **Test data** — ABN `74 591 200 760` (valid check digit, shown in the hint) so testers can pass BR-01 without a lookup. No prefill button, to keep the "not sample data" acceptance criterion honest.
- **Receipt/timestamp** — format `AS-YYMM-XXXX-NNNN`, generated client-side; date/time from the device clock.
- **Extras** — "Edit" jumps from review back to any step (data preserved), and a "Start a new statement" reset.

**One real bug found and fixed during verification:** `.summary`/`.calc` have `overflow:hidden`, which gives them a zero automatic minimum size as grid items — the design system's `.field-stack` grid was squashing them to ~57px and clipping the review content. Fixed with `grid-auto-rows: max-content` on my scroll wrapper (`screens.css` untouched).

Nothing outside `prototype-live/` was modified — `assets/screens.css`, `prototype/`, `prototype-v2/`, `testing/` and `brd/` show no diff. (`go.ps1` shows as modified from before this session started, at 5:02 PM.)



